# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Node
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# Browser-test build output (esbuild bundles the adapter mount entries here on demand)
browser/.build/

# .NET build output (Blazor RCL + examples)
bin/
obj/

# Editor
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# Local agent/session state (scheduler locks, SDD scratch, etc.)
.claude/
.superpowers/

# improvement-notes/ is intentionally NOT ignored, so local project/client notes stay
# @-mentionable in Claude Code. A pre-commit hook (.git/hooks/pre-commit) blocks
# committing them, because this repo is PUBLIC, so those notes must never be pushed.

# NOTE: dist/ is intentionally committed so projects can import
# freeday.tokens.css / freeday.css directly without running a build.

# Local project/client notes. IGNORED since 2026-10-26: 26 files accumulated and every
# `git status` carried an `?? improvement-notes/` line. They stay on disk and stay readable by
# path, so an agent can still open them; what they lose is `git status` noise and some tooling
# that honours this file. Whether a note was acted on is recorded in NEXT-UP.md, which is tracked;
# the folder itself was never the record. The pre-commit hook still blocks them as a second line
# of defence, because this repo is PUBLIC and the notes carry client identifiers.
improvement-notes/
